KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced as int: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
When the call's type is needed, the placeholder return type of the member
function template is deduced with the condition `choice<T>.strategy == 1'
(a static data member template of class type of the enclosing class) not
evaluated, so the discarded `return 1.0' fixes the type as double.  The
same condition in a function with a declared return type, or naming a
namespace-scope variable template, is evaluated.  On MSVC this makes
ranges::iter_move return void for `int *&', so indirectly_readable<int *>
and every iterator concept above it are false (std::span's iterator
constructor, views::take).
